  "survivor_baseline_note": "Recorded from the first measurement of this suite that was not broken. The run before it reported {Survived: 4616, Timeout: 309, Killed: 1} because mull-runner was given --include-not-covered and no --coverage-info: with no profile data it cannot tell reached code from unreached, so it mutated translation units the 22 test functions never call and reported them all as survived. With LLVM profdata from both binaries the corpus is 546 in-scope mutants, of which 340 are killed and 202 survive -- a score of 0.6273, close to the 60.6% the mechanical Python sweep put on this repository's hand-written corpus. None of these 202 is accepted as correct. One was verified by hand outside the tool: changing `xb + i * dim` to `xb + i / dim` at math_space.cpp:53 breaks which row every subsequent read addresses, and the whole kernel suite still reports 'All kernel tests passed!'. The same tree does detect a broken kernel -- inverting AriaOpRelu::scalar aborts test_relu on its first assert -- so the suite is real, and these are behaviours it does not check rather than a measurement artifact.",
